# UniVault

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root for the full briefing. Key rules:

- UniVault is CLI-first: `univault`, `moodle-archive`, `moodle-setup`,
  `ed-archive`, `ed-lessons`, `univault-normalize`.
- `scan` discovers only; `sync` downloads only when the user explicitly asks.
- Remote platforms are read-only; never post, submit, or bypass stealth content.
- Never read, print, or commit `~/.config/univault/moodle-cookie` or Ed tokens.
- Archives live under the user's `learning_root` (default `~/courses`), not in
  this repository.

Common commands:

```bash
univault status
univault sync --dry-run
moodle-archive scan --dest ~/courses/_scan --learning-root ~/courses --json
moodle-archive sync --from-scan ~/courses/_scan/_state/scan-latest.json --course-id <course-id>
```
